IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wiv-dates`

-- Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic), formerly the Wage Theft Act 2020 -- the law the seat module uses: what
-- became of the repealed provisions (does-not-arise answers that name the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025), the s 3 meaning
-- of "worker", the s 69A meaning of detriment and threat, the s 77 circumstances in which information may be disclosed,
-- the s 71(2) duty of a government agency to answer the Inspectorate as one regulative rule with its trace helper, and
-- the table of offences and penalties. The questions are in wiv-seat.l4.
--
-- The Act's terms are kept, each with a plain gloss. Judgments the Act leaves to someone else ("reasonably necessary",
-- "satisfied that it is in the public interest", "good faith", "reasonable belief", "as appropriate") are inputs, never
-- decided here. Terms borrowed from other Acts ("public construction within the meaning of the Project Development and
-- Construction Management Act 1994", "government agency or body") are asked as facts.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Workforce
-- Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020, Version No. 005 (17 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 -- shared rules`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`as an answer` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `The repealed provisions`

-- The provisions the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) repealed, with the section of that Act that repealed
-- each (the side notes of the deposited version). All of ss 4 to 34 of that Act commenced on 12 December 2025 (endnotes).
-- The deposited version does not carry the repealed text; the glosses of Parts 2 and 4 are from the side notes, the
-- endnotes' long title ("offences relating to the theft of employee entitlements and the keeping of records relating to
-- employee entitlements") and the definitions the same Act repealed (employee entitlement offence, employee entitlement
-- record, inspector, withhold).
DECLARE `Former provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1(a) -- the purpose of creating the wage theft offences`
    `s 5`
    `Part 2 -- the wage theft offences (ss 6 to 18)`
    `s 20(1)(c) to (e) -- former functions of the Inspectorate`
    `s 21(2)`
    `Part 4 -- inspectors and their powers (ss 32 to 62)`
    `Part 5 Division 1 (ss 63 to 65)`
    `s 66`
    `s 67`
    `s 68`
    `s 69`
    `Part 5 Division 3 (the former ss 71 to 73)`
    `s 76`
    `s 78`

-- The section of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 that repealed it (side notes).
GIVEN p IS A `Former provision`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the repealing section of the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `s 1(a) -- the purpose of creating the wage theft offences` THEN 4
    WHEN `s 5` THEN 6
    WHEN `Part 2 -- the wage theft offences (ss 6 to 18)` THEN 7
    WHEN `s 20(1)(c) to (e) -- former functions of the Inspectorate` THEN 11
    WHEN `s 21(2)` THEN 12
    WHEN `Part 4 -- inspectors and their powers (ss 32 to 62)` THEN 20
    WHEN `Part 5 Division 1 (ss 63 to 65)` THEN 21
    WHEN `s 66` THEN 22
    WHEN `s 67` THEN 23
    WHEN `s 68` THEN 24
    WHEN `s 69` THEN 25
    WHEN `Part 5 Division 3 (the former ss 71 to 73)` THEN 27
    WHEN `s 76` THEN 30
    WHEN `s 78` THEN 32

-- The does-not-arise answers. Each names the amending Act. The middle answer is NOTHING-kind (*outside the sources*):
-- between 1 July 2021 and 11 December 2025 the provision was in force, but its text is not in the deposited version, and
-- whether it still reaches conduct of that time turns on the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 and any s 83
-- regulations, neither deposited (finding 2).
DECLARE `What the Act says about it now` IS ONE OF
    `it does not arise: repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025`
    `not answered here: in force on that day, but repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025, and its text is not in the deposited version`
    `it does not arise: the Wage Theft Act 2020 was not yet in operation (it came into operation on 1 July 2021, s 2(2))`

-- Every former provision commenced on 1 July 2021 (s 2(2); endnotes) and was repealed on 12 December 2025 (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it now`
`what the Act says now about a repealed provision on` `the day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` `is on or after` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change`
           THEN `it does not arise: repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025`
           IF `the day` `is before` `the day the Act came into operation`
           THEN `it does not arise: the Wage Theft Act 2020 was not yet in operation (it came into operation on 1 July 2021, s 2(2))`
           OTHERWISE `not answered here: in force on that day, but repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025, and its text is not in the deposited version`

§§ `s 3 -- worker and workplace`

-- s 3(1) "worker means a person who is or was (a) employed on a paid or voluntary basis to work at, or in relation to, a
-- workplace; or (b) engaged as an independent contractor to work at, or in relation to, a workplace".
DECLARE `How I am or was engaged` IS ONE OF
    `employed on a paid basis`
    `employed on a voluntary basis`
    `engaged as an independent contractor`
    `engaged in none of these ways`

-- s 3(1) "workplace includes residential premises where work is carried out, but does not include a part of any premises
-- that is the domestic home of a person". The "includes" leaves the ordinary meaning open: whether another place is a
-- workplace is asked.
DECLARE `Where the work is` IS ONE OF
    `at or in relation to a workplace that is not residential premises`
    `at or in relation to residential premises where work is carried out, outside any part that is someone's domestic home`
    `only in a part of premises that is someone's domestic home`
    `not at or in relation to any workplace`

-- A "means" definition: no head, JUST FALSE. The domestic home part is a flat negative of "workplace" (fork F2).
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I am or was engaged`, `where` IS A `Where the work is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- worker` `how` `where` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`an engagement s 3 names` AND `at or in relation to a workplace`)
    WHERE
        `an engagement s 3 names` MEANS (NOT (`how` EQUALS `engaged in none of these ways`))
        `at or in relation to a workplace` MEANS
                `where` EQUALS `at or in relation to a workplace that is not residential premises`
            OR  `where` EQUALS `at or in relation to residential premises where work is carried out, outside any part that is someone's domestic home`

§§ `s 69A -- detriment and threats`

-- s 69A(6) "detriment (a) includes (i) injury; (ii) intimidation or harassment; (iii) ostracism; (iv) damage to or loss
-- of property; (b) does not include (i) discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in or in connection with
-- employment; (ii) dismissal from, or prejudice in or in connection with, employment; (iii) disciplinary proceedings in or
-- in connection with employment."
DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `injury`
    `intimidation or harassment`
    `ostracism`
    `damage to or loss of property`
    `discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in or in connection with employment`
    `dismissal from, or prejudice in or in connection with, employment`
    `disciplinary proceedings in or in connection with employment`
    `some other harm`

-- (a) an open list: some other harm is NOTHING-kind (*open list*); (b) a flat negative: JUST FALSE (finding 4 on overlap).
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69A(6) -- detriment` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `injury` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `intimidation or harassment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `ostracism` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `damage to or loss of property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other harm` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open list: "includes")
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 69A(1)(a) to (f): what the person knows or believes about the other person.
DECLARE `What they knew or believed about me` IS ONE OF
    `I had made a complaint to the Inspectorate`
    `I had provided information about public construction to the Inspectorate`
    `I intended to make, or was considering whether to make, a complaint to the Inspectorate`
    `I intended to provide, or was considering whether to provide, information about public construction to the Inspectorate`
    `I had participated, or was participating, in a process arising from a complaint to the Inspectorate`
    `I intended to participate, or was considering whether to participate, in such a process`
    `none of the s 69A(1) matters`

DECLARE `Done or threatened` IS ONE OF
    `it was done to me`
    `it was threatened`
    `neither`

-- s 69A(3) "A person threatens to cause detriment to another person if the person (a) intends that the other person will
-- believe that the person will cause detriment to the other person; or (b) is reckless as to whether the other person
-- will believe" it. An "if" definition: neither, JUST FALSE. (4) the threat may be by words or conduct, explicit or
-- implicit, and "need not be believed".
GIVEN `intended` IS A BOOLEAN, `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69A(3) -- a threat` `intended` `reckless` MEANS `as an answer` (`intended` OR `reckless`)

§§ `s 77 -- confidentiality`

-- s 77(2) (a) to (f): the circumstances in which a person may disclose information acquired under this Act.
DECLARE `Why it is disclosed` IS ONE OF
    `reasonably necessary for the person to perform their functions or exercise their powers under this Act`
    `in accordance with the Inspectorate's functions under s 20(1)(ib) or (id) (referring public construction matters, advising the Minister)`
    `to a court or VCAT in the course of legal proceedings`
    `under an order of a court or VCAT`
    `to the extent reasonably required to enable the investigation or enforcement of a law of Victoria, another State or Territory or the Commonwealth`
    `with the written consent of the person to whom the information relates`
    `required by law`
    `none of the s 77(2) circumstances`

-- s 77(1) "must not disclose the information unless the disclosure is authorised under this section": an "unless", so
-- no circumstance and no s 77(3) public interest decision is JUST FALSE. Information not obtained under this Act is
-- outside s 77 (*limited by its own wording*), NOTHING.
GIVEN `obtained under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `why` IS A `Why it is disclosed`, `the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77 -- the disclosure is authorised` `obtained under this Act` `why` `the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the public interest` MEANS
    IF (NOT `obtained under this Act`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "under this Act")
    ELSE `as an answer` ((NOT (`why` EQUALS `none of the s 77(2) circumstances`)) OR `the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the public interest`)

§§ `s 71 -- the agency's duty to answer the Inspectorate`

DECLARE `What became of the agency's duty` IS ONE OF
    `the Act puts no duty on the agency on these facts`
    `the Inspectorate specified no time: the Act says only within a reasonable time`
    `provided in time`
    `not provided in time`
    `the time to provide it is still running`

DECLARE `Agency party` IS ONE OF
    `the government agency or body`

DECLARE `Agency act` IS ONE OF
    `provide the notification or information requested (s 71(2))`

-- s 71(2) "A government agency or body that receives a request under subsection (1) must provide the required
-- notification or information within a reasonable time, as specified by the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria." Counted in
-- plain days from the request (fork F8).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Agency party` `Agency act`
`the agency must answer the Inspectorate in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the government agency or body`
    MUST `provide the notification or information requested (s 71(2))`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the government agency or body` BECAUSE "the government agency or body did not provide the notification or information within the time the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria specified (s 71(2) of the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020)"

-- The trace helper, in the shape of the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 encoding's. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on
-- an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where it was provided, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late;
-- where it was not, the helper asks whether providing it today would still be in time.
GIVEN `the days allowed`       IS A NUMBER
      `it has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time it was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the agency's duty`
`what became of the agency's duty to answer` `the days allowed` `it has been done` `the time it was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the agency must answer the Inspectorate in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `the government agency or body` `provide the notification or information requested (s 71(2))` `the time it was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `provided in time`
         OTHERWISE `not provided in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the agency must answer the Inspectorate in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the government agency or body` `provide the notification or information requested (s 71(2))` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the time to provide it is still running`
         OTHERWISE `not provided in time`

§§ `Offences and penalties`

-- The offences left in the Act. The value of a penalty unit is fixed under the Monetary Units Act 2004, not deposited:
-- the answer is in penalty units.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 69A -- causing or threatening detriment because of a complaint to the Inspectorate`
    `s 70(1) -- giving information to the Inspectorate believed false or misleading`
    `s 70(2) -- producing a document to the Inspectorate known to be false or misleading`
    `s 77(1) -- disclosing information obtained under this Act without authority`

-- s 69A: "Level 5 fine (1200 penalty units maximum) or level 5 imprisonment (10 years maximum) or both", one figure for
-- anyone. s 70(1), (2): "In the case of a body corporate, level 5 fine (1200 penalty units maximum); In any other case,
-- level 7 imprisonment (2 years maximum)". s 77(1): "75 penalty units". Where the Act gives no fine (s 70 for a natural
-- person) or no separate corporate figure (ss 69A, 77) it is silent, and a general rule outside the Act (the Sentencing
-- Act 1991, not deposited) may supply one: NOTHING-kind *silent* (finding 7).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum fine in penalty units for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 69A -- causing or threatening detriment because of a complaint to the Inspectorate` THEN `natural person figure only` 1200
    WHEN `s 77(1) -- disclosing information obtained under this Act without authority` THEN `natural person figure only` 75
    OTHERWISE `the s 70 figure`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `natural` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        `natural person figure only` `natural` MEANS IF `a body corporate` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `natural` -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no body corporate figure)
        `the s 70 figure` MEANS IF `a body corporate` THEN JUST 1200 ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no fine for a natural person)

-- Imprisonment, natural persons only: s 69A "10 years" (120 months); s 70 "2 years" (24 months); s 77 none.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `s 69A -- causing or threatening detriment because of a complaint to the Inspectorate` THEN 120
         WHEN `s 77(1) -- disclosing information obtained under this Act without authority` THEN 0
         OTHERWISE 24
